OracleAdapter.rescueFunds

when called by the owner with an ERC20 token and sufficient token balance
    it transfers ERC20 tokens to the TREASURY_WALLET
        expect TREASURY_WALLET token balance to increase by _amount
        expect contract token balance to decrease by _amount
    it emits FundsRescued event
        expect event with correct parameters

when called by the owner with _token == address(0) (native ETH) and _amount <= contract ETH balance
    it transfers native ETH to the TREASURY_WALLET
        expect TREASURY_WALLET ETH balance to increase by _amount
        expect contract ETH balance to decrease by _amount
    it emits FundsRescued event
        expect event with correct parameters

when _amount is zero
    it reverts
        expect revert with Errors.ZeroAmount

when _token == address(0) and _amount > contract ETH balance
    it reverts
        expect revert with Errors.InsufficientBalance
    it does not change state
        expect no change in TREASURY_WALLET and contract ETH balances

when ERC20 token path but contract lacks sufficient token balance or token transfer fails
    it reverts
        expect revert from SafeERC20.safeTransfer (bubble up)
    it does not change state
        expect no change in TREASURY_WALLET and contract token balances

when called by a non-owner
    it reverts
        expect revert with OwnableUnauthorizedAccount including the caller
    it does not change state
        expect no change in TREASURY_WALLET or contract balances
